   <item>
       <widget class="QCheckBox" name="discardTerminalDeletes">
           <property name="text">
               <string>Discard terminal deletes</string>
           </property>
           <property name="toolTip">
               <string>Drop tag removals instead of writing them into chunks.

                   A terminal delete is a tag whose history ended in a removal. It collapses to that removal alone,
                   never to a paired add, so at import it removes a mapping this import never made. If the tags in your
                   database came only from the PTR, every one of them is a no-op, and discarding them makes the chunks
                   smaller and the import faster.

                   Leave this off if you are layering the PTR onto records that already have tags from elsewhere, such
                   as a Hydrus import: there the removals are meaningful.
               </string>
           </property>
       </widget>
   </item>
